Payload tools: every member under the payload's bin directory is unpacked into a cache
keyed by the binary's size and mtime, and that directory goes first on PATH before any
makefile is read, so recipes, $(shell) and a payload's boot script all find the tools
the build carries. A recursive make sees the directory already first and does nothing.
AMK_NO_PATH in the environment turns it off; a build without a payload bin is unchanged.

--- a/src/main.c
+++ b/src/main.c
@@ -1373,7 +1373,95 @@
   return MAKE_FAILURE;
 }
 #endif
